# Configuration with real values. .env.example is the committed template;
# everything it is copied to is not.
#
# This service holds credentials that move money — the bank's, the card
# provider's, and the master key that decrypts every property's payout
# destination. None of it belongs in version control, and a leak is not
# undone by a later commit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# A filled-in Postman environment holds a live API key and a platform key, both
# of which move money or read every property's payment records. The template
# beside it carries placeholders and is the one that gets committed.
postman/*.postman_environment.json
!postman/ptep_gateway_local.postman_environment.json
!postman/ptep_gateway_production.template.postman_environment.json

# Signing keys and certificates, however they are named.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
private-key*
*private_key*

# Build output. The module is `example.com/fiber-mvc`, so `go build` with no
# -o leaves a binary called this in the working directory.
fiber-mvc
/main
/bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Local scratch
*.log
/tmp/
.DS_Store

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
